<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Report on “</strong><strong>Three-Day Workshop on Automation using PLC &amp; SCADA</strong><strong>”</strong> at Department of Mechanical Engineering, ATMECE, Mysuru</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Department of Mechanical Engineering, ATMECE is organized Three-Day Workshop on Automation using PLC &amp; SCADA for the Final year students of Mechanical Engineering from <strong>15<sup>th</sup> to 17<sup>th</sup> December 2022</strong> in association with Vidyut Automation, Mysuru. The training program was intended to enrich student’s knowledge in the field of Automation. Workshop also included hands-on session where in students got a chance to work on PLC training Kit. 49 students had registered for the workshop.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">The objectives intended for the workshop are as follows.</p>

<ol style="text-align: justify;">
 	<li style="text-align: justify;">To develop skill in the field of Automation</li>
 	<li style="text-align: justify;">To monitor and control equipment used in process automation.</li>
 	<li style="text-align: justify;">To control and maintain efficiency, distribute data for smarter decisions and communicate system issues to help mitigate downtime.</li>
</ol>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><img class="aligncenter wp-image-9831 size-medium" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/me111-300x200.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="200"></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Inauguration of Workshop by Chief Guests</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">The program was inaugurated by Dr. L Basavaraj, Principal, ATMECE in the presence of chief guest Dr. M. S. Govinde Gowda, Dean Academics, ATMECE, Resource person Mr. Shashikiran M, Managing Director, Vidyut Automation, Mysuru. &nbsp;Dr. L.Basavaraj appreciated the intention of the workshop as the program would help the students to identify the career in the field of Automation.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Dr. M.S. Govinde Gowda expressed that it is high time to acquire knowledge about the interdisciplinary and emerging technologies so that students will have wider exposure in the present Job market. Also, he mentioned that students have to gain knowledge beyond the curriculum and enhance the competitiveness in the field of Automation.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Dr. Srinivasa K, HoD, Mechanical Engineering department, greeted the dignitaries in his welcome speech and mentioned the importance of the special knowledge and Skills along with the curriculum.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Dr. Chethan.S, Asst. Prof, Dept of ME, convenor of the program, briefed about the workshop by mentioning the activities and hands on sessions planned for three-day workshop. He briefed the Objectives designed to enhance the knowledge in the field of automation and expected Outcomes of the workshop.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">Mr. Anilkumar K, Asst. Professor, Dept. of ME, briefed about the Resource person and Mr. Rohith S Asst. Professor, Dept. of ME, rendered Vote of thanks to the gathering.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Day 1 Morning Session</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">The first day of the workshop was based on training on Allen Bradley MicroLogix 1400 PLC. The morning session included presentation on Basic gates, Automation, PLC introduction and Architecture. The resource person gave detailed lecture on Allen Bradley MicroLogix 1400 PLC. The hands-on session on the mentioned kit was carried out in the afternoon session.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><img class="aligncenter wp-image-9832 size-medium" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/mee222-300x225.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="225"></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Presentation on Basic gates and Ladder diagram by Resource Person</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Day 1 Afternoon Session </strong></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;">The hands-on session included familiarization on Allen Bradley PLC programming software followed by working on the following modules using the kit.</p>

<ul style="text-align: justify;">
 	<li style="text-align: justify;">Basic Instructions and worked examples on NO, NC, Coil, Latch, Unlatch, Time.</li>
 	<li style="text-align: justify;">Communication between PLC and PC using RS 232 and Ethernet cable</li>
 	<li style="text-align: justify;">Program Uploading, Downloading, Run, Online editing</li>
</ul>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><img class="alignleft wp-image-9833 size-medium" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/mee3-300x226.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="226"><img class="alignleft wp-image-9834 size-medium" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/mee4-300x225.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="225"></p>
&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Day -1 Hands on Session using Allen Bradley PLC programming software</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Day 2 Morning Session</strong></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </strong>The second day of the workshop was based on training on Factory Talk View Studio SCADA. The resource person gave detailed lecture on SCADA and the hand on session SCADA software was carried out in the afternoon session.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Day 2 Afternoon Session </strong></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><img class="alignleft wp-image-9835 size-medium" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/mee5-300x225.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="225"><img class="alignleft wp-image-9836 size-medium" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/mee6-300x225.jpg" alt="" width="300" height="225"></p>
&nbsp;

&nbsp;

