<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;"><strong>ATME Students Develop Low Cost Coin Operated Water Vending Machine</strong></span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">The final year Mechanical Engineering students of ATME College of Engineering, Mysuru – Mr. D V Raghu, Mr. Gayaz Mohammed, Mr. Md Mohiyuddin Shariff and Mr,. MD Yaseen Ahmed as a part of their final year project work, has developed a low cost, portable, compact sized, economical and simple Water Vending Machine which accepts coin and dispenses a glass of water from pre purified 20 lts which is available in market.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">This Project was selected for financial funding from Karnataka State Council for Science and Technology (KSCST) and recognize as “Outstanding project” and Awarded with “Project or the Year” award by KSCST.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">The subject knowledge gained in their course and under the guidance of Mr. Rakshith N, Assistant Professor, Department of Mechanical Engineering and Mr. Chandan G N, Assistant Professor, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, they have successfully completed the work at a cost of 8000/- RS.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">The students Effort has been hailed by many including the industry people, Public. The Principal, Staff members and Management congratulated them on their feat.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;"><strong>New India Pledge</strong></span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">As per the directions of the AICTE, regarding celebration of 70 years of Independence and 75 years of Quit India Movement at our institute, the staff and Students of the Department of mechanical engineering took the New India Pledge on 9.08.2017.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;"><strong><img class="size-full wp-image-5734 aligncenter" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/pldge_india_baner-1.png" alt="" width="810" height="250">A Report on Road safety awareness Program “Yuva janara nadige –Rasthe surakshateya kadege”</strong></span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">The Department of Mechanical Engineering of ATME College of Engineering actively participated in road awareness program organized by Government of Karnataka Regional Transportation department, Mysore on 26th of February 2017 at ‘ Ovals ground’, Mysore. The program was presided by Honorable District incharge minister Dr. H C Mahadevappa, National athlete Mr. Arjun Devaiah, District Regional Transport officer, Superintend of Police Mr. Ravi D Channannavar.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">The program was inaugurated by District incharge minister Dr. H c Mahadevappa. National athlete Mr. Arjun Devaiah recited the pledge and all our students and faculties actively participated in road march.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;"><img class="size-full wp-image-5735 aligncenter" src="https://old.atme.edu.in/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/me3-1.jpg" alt="" width="400" height="250">Road march route was started from Ovals ground by covering major roads 100feet road, corporation office road, DD Urs Road and finally reached Ovals ground.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;"><strong>Pledge against corruption</strong></span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: #000000;">As a part of taking pledge against corruption initiated by the central government, The Dept of Mechanical Engineering of ATMECE, Mysore initiated the drive on 04-05-2016 across various semesters. A total of around 600 students took the oath to fight against corruption and to be a constructive citizen for the development of the country as per the vision for 2020. The drive was initiated by the senior staff of Mechanical Engineering Dept guided by the HOD Dr. Ratnakar.</span></p>
